    "moon": "nothing in you ranks the two. that is the ordinary solution — a first family and a second, one call that outranks the other — and no part of you has ever produced it, so both claims stand at full height. which one you drive to on the night both go wrong gets settled by proximity, and that has stood in for a decision every time.",
    "pull": "two households have been told, by your arrival, that you are the one who comes. the promise was made twice, in the same words, by somebody carrying no order of precedence.",
    "tension": "the two people with the best evidence of your reliability are the two who call you unreliable. each of them has a night when you were there before anyone, and a night when you were unreachable and vague about it afterwards. the vagueness is the one part you have ever controlled. neither has been given the other address, so what each holds is a person who is either first through the door or nowhere, on no pattern anybody can find.",
    "cost": "most people run one of these; you have carried two intact for twenty years, and each side has had the whole of you in its worst hour, and neither has been short-changed on any night. one night in twenty came with both. whichever you did not reach has that night filed under something you cannot correct — the only accurate reading either of them has ever taken of you."
