    "moon": "both ends have to pull or the distance opens, so The Thread makes a haul of it rather than a store, maintained in two directions, for years. the one letting go has to go on feeling it is still his; the one coming has to feel something already waiting for her. neither registers a third party in it, because a line under load carries weight and shows no effort.",
    "pull": "the record will say he handed it to her. eleven years happened inside that verb, and no account of this has a line where they could be written.",
    "tension": "nothing went wrong is the whole of what gets said, and it gets said warmly. the one who arrived believes she took it from the one who left, her thanks go there, and from inside her account that is what happened. the interval would only have been visible if it had failed — a lost year, a gap somebody fell through — and each of those was stopped by the same holding that removed the reason to mention it.",
    "cost": "two things that would have come apart in the stretch between them stay attached instead, and neither end spends a year knowing there was a stretch. the pull was the whole of your position. when the ends touch, what has held you upright for eleven years lets go from both sides on one afternoon, and nothing accrued on your side of it while you were the thing in the middle."
