    "sun": "resolving into six takes years of somebody's attention, and arriving first spends your life inside the first ten minutes of things. so the count gets taken at the door, at speed, by people standing at the furthest they will ever be from you — and one is what a door produces. hundreds of accurate readings of you exist out there, all of them taken off a stand-in.",
    "moon": "arriving first never came with the second half, and here the second half lives in another part of the building. the one who commits on the mat is rarely the one who can do the work, so a handover happens mid-sentence, at speed, inside the emergency. the household gets a rescue that changes hands while it is running, and nothing to call the difference it felt.",
    "pull": "the quickest of you commits the other five before they have finished hearing the phone. every promise you have kept was kept by somebody who was not in the doorway.",
    "tension": "you were different at the start is what comes, from people who cannot name what changed. the one who does beginnings does nothing else, and steps off once a thing is underway; whoever picks it up has never stood in a doorway in their life. no withdrawal has occurred. it lands as one every time, and the warmth that opened the account gets used as evidence against the rest of you.",
    "cost": "beginnings get a specialist. whoever needs you at the start meets a part of you that does nothing but start, is therefore never tired of them, which nobody on a fourth attempt has ever managed to fake. that one never learns how a single thing ended. the arrivals are the whole of its life, hundreds of them, and the results were collected by the others."
