    "sun": "one is what a stranger gets, and a stranger is what everyone stays. the six do not hide — resolving them is slow work, done by somebody with tenure, and tenure is the one thing nothing in your life produces. so the misreading holds everywhere, permanently, and it holds without a single act of concealment on your part. rooms you were warm in for a year still keep a one-person record of you.",
    "moon": "the front of you goes first and goes fast, and the pleasure runs out at the moment a thing is known. a person is the same shape as any other subject that way. so you leave at almost exactly the depth where the second one of you would have started to show, every time, and the leaving has always had a real reason attached.",
    "pull": "the count gets taken early every time, by somebody still inside their first year of you, and it comes back one. no witness has ever been in the room with the second of you.",
    "tension": "you never let anyone in is the charge, and it comes from people who were let in and found nobody sitting there. nothing was withheld. the door was open the whole time and the room was empty, because whatever was interesting had moved to the next street. the version they take away is small and fond and one person deep, and arguing with it means claiming there is more, which is what everybody claims.",
    "cost": "almost nothing you know came secondhand — you went and found out, in person, about more of the world than most people get near in a life. what you are made of gets settled by heat, and heat means staying in the room past the part that was interesting. so the world is known at first hand and you are known by report."
