    "tension": "going backwards is what it gets called, and the people saying it can date the last time — the same argument, the same want, the same person you were told to leave alone. from outside, someone settled losing ground they covered a decade ago is the clearest picture of relapse available. the true account, that a part of you went down and has come up at its original age, is not something anyone can be asked to work with.",
    "cost": "an instrument put down for fifteen years comes back to hand at the standard it was left at, and a person you loved is still loved at the original temperature by whoever was holding that. nothing here is finally spent. the same clause preserves the rest — shame from one night at nineteen arrives decades later undamaged, and nothing has worn it down enough to argue with."
