    "sun": "heat is what settles the count. a hard year takes whichever of you was never carrying anything, and everybody who comes out the far side of one knows something they did not know going in. that finding never lands here. whatever the year burned off is still on file, at the resolution it had on its last evening out, held by the one of you who happened to be watching.",
    "moon": "the noticing is done by one of the several, and it turned inward early, since there is more in here to read than most rooms offer. it has looked properly at each of the others — the seventeen-year-old, the one who ran a household badly for four years — and having looked, it cannot put any of them away. nothing in this building is ever past tense.",
