    "tension": "you never move on is the charge, and it is a soft version of what they mean. something from nine years ago comes out of you intact — the wording, the room, the order it happened in — because the one who has it never stopped having it. nobody keeps a record at that grain by accident, so the accuracy is heard as a case you have been building, quietly, the whole time.",
    "cost": "nothing in your history has to be reconstructed. you can say which of you did a thing, in what year, and what it did to the house, at a fidelity nobody has about their own twenties. none of it can be set down. other people get to lose a bad decade; yours has a keeper, and the keeper lives here and answers when the others are asleep."
