    "sun": "the chair was cut to hold one occupant and there are six of you, so the fit gets tested six separate times, privately, by whichever one has it that week. no comparison is available — none of you attends another's turn. from any distance the picture is a single person carrying something heavy without visible effort, and inside it the same unanswered question runs down six lines that never cross.",
    "moon": "the carriage will not allow a flinch, and it holds in both directions — outward, so no room ever learns which of you is the one currently unsure; inward, so none of the six can tell the others either. what makes a household stand up straighter around you is the same mechanism that leaves every one of you alone with a question about the seat.",
