    "tension": "uneven is the kind word. the harder one arrives when a piece is good enough to be worth doubting, and somebody who has studied the rest says, carefully, that it does not sound like you. they are right about the evidence. what would answer them is an account of six makers sharing one name and one pair of hands, and anybody who says that out loud has already lost the argument.",
    "cost": "range no single maker gets near — six settled styles, none of them borrowed. a name is the thing that cannot be built out of it. reputations run on recognisable work, and yours is recognisable six ways, so people remember a piece and not a person, and whichever of you made the best thing on the shelf holds no more standing here than the one who made the worst."
