    "tension": "somebody who loves you spends a bad negotiation waiting for the other one to come out. they have watched you be six kinds of person, so a hard one is a reasonable thing to expect. it does not arrive, and what they take from that is a decision you made to stay soft. six separate evenings have now settled it for six separate people, each of whom met a different one of you and had the same evening.",
    "cost": "what meets a person here is skilled and entirely uncovered, which is why things get told to you that do not get told elsewhere. no harder version can be sent in instead. whatever gets agreed at a table goes on the whole house, so five of you wake into terms fixed by an evening they were not at, by the least protected person in the room."
