    "sun": "you have all of it: what he is doing, roughly when it started, and why. the evidence is a pause of the wrong length and a way of saying somebody's name, which produces nothing anybody could be shown. nothing about it has weathered either, so the position has not softened in ten years — you are the person in the family who knows, and the one who cannot demonstrate it.",
    "moon": "the one instrument you have is room, so the finding gets converted into it. an evening cleared for no stated reason. a question left wide enough to take anything. a silence held four seconds past comfort, cut to fit what you saw. whatever went into that space would bind him the moment he put it there, which is why he does not, and why you keep cutting the opening anyway.",
    "pull": "every opening you have made him was cut to fit a thing you will not say. he has walked through ten years of them without once seeing the shape.",
    "tension": "easiest person in the family to talk to is the standing verdict, and it is accurate, and nobody has talked to you about this. an opening asks nothing — that is what makes it safe and what makes it useless here. ten years of them have been declined by a man who does not know he declined anything, because from where he sat each one was an ordinary evening with somebody who was fond of him.",
    "cost": "you can give a person the exact conditions for saying the hardest sentence of their life — no pressure, no cornering, no charge for walking away from it. room carries no content. so the reading you took in one afternoon has gone out ten times as a cleared evening, been mistaken for hospitality ten times, and comes home with you intact every time."
